WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:02.734
-Our first guest tonight
is the host of

00:00:02.734 --> 00:00:04.300
the Emmy- and
Peabody Award-winning show

00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:06.000
"Last Week Tonight,"
which airs Sunday nights

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:07.968
on HBO and streams on HBO Max.

00:00:07.968 --> 00:00:11.100
Please welcome back to the show
our friend John Oliver.

00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:13.000
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:00:27.801 --> 00:00:30.801
Welcome back.
-It's very nice to be back.

00:00:30.801 --> 00:00:33.300
-It's been a while.
It's been a while in the studio.

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:34.868
We've talked via Zoom
a few times.

00:00:34.868 --> 00:00:38.300
-Yes. It's been almost
exactly two years

00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:40.000
since I've been in this studio.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:42.400
-And if people do the math,
that's right before --

00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:45.634
That's sort of the eve of when
the whole city shut down.

00:00:45.634 --> 00:00:47.334
And looking back at
our interview,

00:00:47.334 --> 00:00:48.667
do you think we played it right?

00:00:48.667 --> 00:00:51.200
Do you think we had the
right tenor for the moment?

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:54.434
-I don't know how many people
here regularly watch interviews

00:00:54.434 --> 00:00:58.234
that we do from two years ago,
but during that,

00:00:58.234 --> 00:00:59.868
we were having some goofs...

00:00:59.868 --> 00:01:01.968
-We were goofing hard.

00:01:01.968 --> 00:01:06.234
-...about the fact that
the first coronavirus case

00:01:06.234 --> 00:01:08.901
had just been confirmed
in New York City.

00:01:08.901 --> 00:01:12.033
And goof away, we were,
you know,

00:01:12.033 --> 00:01:14.501
slightly out of nervousness,
I think.

00:01:14.501 --> 00:01:15.834
-Sure, sure, sure.
Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:01:15.834 --> 00:01:20.033
That's what what I was doing.
-Certainly. Certainly.

00:01:20.033 --> 00:01:22.434
Not a zero amount
of misplaced confidence.

00:01:22.434 --> 00:01:25.634
I remember leaving here
thinking, "Goofs well done,

00:01:25.634 --> 00:01:26.634
fun was had."

00:01:26.634 --> 00:01:27.701
-Absolutely.

00:01:27.701 --> 00:01:29.267
-I got back to
my apartment building,

00:01:29.267 --> 00:01:31.000
and there was
an ambulance outside,

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:34.200
and I thought, "I have [bleep]
misjudged this situation."

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:35.534
Oh [bleep]

00:01:35.534 --> 00:01:38.133
-Yeah.
-And it hadn't even been on TV.

00:01:38.133 --> 00:01:39.801
I was literally sitting
at home thinking,

00:01:39.801 --> 00:01:42.501
"I don't even want to watch
what I just said,

00:01:42.501 --> 00:01:44.934
because I think things
have shifted a little."

00:01:44.934 --> 00:01:47.934
So, it is very nice to be back.
-Yeah.

00:01:47.934 --> 00:01:49.801
-And I'm going to be
very careful with how

00:01:49.801 --> 00:01:52.501
confidently
I'll predict anything

00:01:52.501 --> 00:01:53.601
while sitting in this chair.

00:01:53.601 --> 00:01:55.601
-I think it's very wise
for both of us

00:01:55.601 --> 00:01:56.667
to get well out of
the prediction game.

00:01:56.667 --> 00:01:58.601
-Yes. It is nice. It is nice.

00:01:58.601 --> 00:02:00.968
It's nice to see you
dress down for your show.

00:02:00.968 --> 00:02:02.400
-Well, it was very nice
to have you.

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:03.767
I mean, we really
dodged a bullet,

00:02:03.767 --> 00:02:05.701
because you basically are
wearing one of my outfits --

00:02:05.701 --> 00:02:08.534
one of my five outfits.

00:02:08.534 --> 00:02:10.801
-I think if you have
no sartorial confidence

00:02:10.801 --> 00:02:13.901
or imagination,
it's either this, this,

00:02:13.901 --> 00:02:17.200
some variation, mildly,
of colors within them,

00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:18.834
but, essentially, you're not
gonna risk anything else,

00:02:18.834 --> 00:02:20.601
because, fundamentally,
you know you can't carry it off.

00:02:20.601 --> 00:02:24.701
-Yeah, no, it's shocking to me
that once I first got out of

00:02:24.701 --> 00:02:26.267
a suit, I'm like,
"Now I can do anything."

00:02:26.267 --> 00:02:27.434
And it's like,
"No, it's just been this."

00:02:27.434 --> 00:02:30.067
Yeah.
-No, you can't. No, you can't.

00:02:30.067 --> 00:02:33.267
-It's like, "Now I'm out of my
cage and into a different cage."

00:02:34.801 --> 00:02:37.968
You, of course,
spent a lot of time in the void.

00:02:37.968 --> 00:02:40.601
And I gave you --
I tipped my cap to you early on.

00:02:40.601 --> 00:02:41.701
-You did.

00:02:41.701 --> 00:02:43.267
-Because you figured out
a way to just

00:02:43.267 --> 00:02:44.567
nail the look right off the bat.

00:02:44.567 --> 00:02:47.567
-Yeah, we got lucky,
because when we were initially

00:02:47.567 --> 00:02:50.300
doing a panic move to
a studio in New Jersey,

00:02:50.300 --> 00:02:52.567
when we couldn't do it from our
studio, we just thought,

00:02:52.567 --> 00:02:54.267
"Let's put a white backdrop in."

00:02:54.267 --> 00:02:56.834
And then that worked out
pretty well,

00:02:56.834 --> 00:02:58.367
so let's roll with
the white backdrop

00:02:58.367 --> 00:03:00.868
so I don't invite
people into my life at all.

00:03:00.868 --> 00:03:01.868
-Yeah.

00:03:01.868 --> 00:03:06.167
-You, of course,
had books, children,

00:03:06.167 --> 00:03:07.734
in that order.

00:03:07.734 --> 00:03:08.968
-Yeah.

00:03:08.968 --> 00:03:14.467
Everybody -- I just opened
my world up to criticism

00:03:14.467 --> 00:03:15.834
from people watching the show.

00:03:15.834 --> 00:03:17.133
-That's the thing --
I think it's best for me

00:03:17.133 --> 00:03:21.234
to go with a kind of antiseptic,
austere background

00:03:21.234 --> 00:03:23.300
that really invites
no questions.

00:03:23.300 --> 00:03:25.534
-I guess it's very clear that
a man who chose that sweater

00:03:25.534 --> 00:03:27.701
was like,
"What about all white?"

00:03:28.934 --> 00:03:30.434
What about just pure --

00:03:30.434 --> 00:03:34.934
-How about white
so you just deal with that?

00:03:34.934 --> 00:03:37.467
-How -- And now you've got half
an audience back.

00:03:37.467 --> 00:03:39.734
-Yes, yeah.
-And we've got the --

00:03:39.734 --> 00:03:41.767
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Oh. That's right.

00:03:41.767 --> 00:03:42.767
-Yeah.

00:03:42.767 --> 00:03:44.968
-I'll accept that
from half of you.

00:03:44.968 --> 00:03:47.167
-So, we got
a full house here now.

00:03:47.167 --> 00:03:48.767
Are you alright with that?
-Yeah, I think I'm fine.

00:03:48.767 --> 00:03:50.133
-Okay.
-We're far enough away.

00:03:50.133 --> 00:03:52.267
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
-That's not even COVID.

00:03:52.267 --> 00:03:54.200
I just like dist--

00:03:54.200 --> 00:03:56.033
-That's just British.
-That's right, exactly.

00:03:56.033 --> 00:03:58.968
I like emotional distance,
as well as physical.

00:03:58.968 --> 00:04:01.601
-Now, you did something that
I immediately had to text you.

00:04:01.601 --> 00:04:04.100
And, I mean, you know,
look, I'll admit --

00:04:04.100 --> 00:04:05.501
I was a little angry with you,

00:04:05.501 --> 00:04:06.801
and I felt like
I could text you.

00:04:06.801 --> 00:04:07.968
-Okay, good.
-Yeah.

00:04:07.968 --> 00:04:10.067
I just wanted to be hon--
You did an interview

00:04:10.067 --> 00:04:11.734
where you said some very nice
things about our show.

00:04:11.734 --> 00:04:13.067
-I like it very much.

00:04:13.067 --> 00:04:15.734
-And you said one of
your favorite things was Wally,

00:04:15.734 --> 00:04:16.734
the cue-card guy,

00:04:16.734 --> 00:04:17.734
off and on camera.

00:04:17.734 --> 00:04:19.200
-I did say that.
-Yeah.

00:04:19.200 --> 00:04:24.167
-And I do see where
you're coming from

00:04:24.167 --> 00:04:28.634
when you say,
"Careful what you're doing here,

00:04:28.634 --> 00:04:30.901
because it's
getting out of hand."

00:04:30.901 --> 00:04:34.601
I saw Wally's appearance
during the monologue.

00:04:34.601 --> 00:04:37.200
I recognize you actually
have a bit of a problem.

00:04:37.200 --> 00:04:38.534
-Yeah.

00:04:38.534 --> 00:04:41.400
-Because it does feel --
One of the things

00:04:41.400 --> 00:04:43.868
I'm enjoying about this show
very much in the moment is

00:04:43.868 --> 00:04:47.901
watching a
slow-motion coup unfold.

00:04:47.901 --> 00:04:49.701
It's all fun.

00:04:49.701 --> 00:04:51.968
It's all fun and games, and then
there's a little too much

00:04:51.968 --> 00:04:55.033
confidence with the way
he delivers a line.

00:04:55.033 --> 00:04:57.200
And watching Wally now,
I feel like

00:04:57.200 --> 00:05:01.467
it's like when you watch
a child get famous.

00:05:01.467 --> 00:05:05.067
Like, initially,
you're happy for them,

00:05:05.067 --> 00:05:07.501
and then you start to worry,
"Where does this end?"

00:05:07.501 --> 00:05:09.367
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:05:09.367 --> 00:05:10.734
No, it's interesting
you say that,

00:05:10.734 --> 00:05:13.100
'cause I do feel like
it's gonna be a bloodless coup.

00:05:13.100 --> 00:05:14.734
-Yes, exactly.

00:05:14.734 --> 00:05:18.100
Either that or Wally
is just hurtling towards

00:05:18.100 --> 00:05:22.534
a cocaine habit
and a show on Peacock.

00:05:23.601 --> 00:05:26.467
-And just all the cards
are just gonna say, "Clip?"

00:05:26.467 --> 00:05:28.501
-That's right.

00:05:28.501 --> 00:05:30.267
-Just roll a clip.
That'll be better.

00:05:30.267 --> 00:05:32.934
Hey, as always, I have a million
more things to ask you about,

00:05:32.934 --> 00:05:34.367
so we'll be right back.

00:05:34.367 --> 00:05:36.300
We'll get -- Let's put Wally --
-There he is. There he is.

00:05:36.300 --> 00:05:39.100
-Oh, look, his best friend.
His best friend.

00:05:39.100 --> 00:05:41.300
We'll be right back with more
from John Oliver.

